# Reduced TS, step 2: NumFreq on the host-relaxed structure (COMPUTATIONAL.md C8).
#
# Geometry: ../job.xyz, the result of step 1 -- the reduced TS seed with the
# reacting core (1-based 129-137) held fixed while the 120-atom host relaxed onto
# the B97-3c surface (host RMSD 0.200 A, core unchanged).
#
# Purpose: (a) the mode picture -- whether the reaction coordinate is the single
# imaginary mode; (b) a central-difference HESSIAN to feed the OptTS in step 3.
# NumFreq, not Freq/Calc_Hess: ORCA's forward-difference Calc_Hess produced 4
# spurious negatives against central-difference NumFreq's 1 on the earlier
# attempt, and sent that OptTS chasing scaffold modes.
#
# NO constraints here -- the Hessian must cover all 137 atoms for the
# unconstrained OptTS that follows.
#
# Next: OptTS with `%geom inhess Read; InHessName "../numfreq/job.hess"`, and
# `%qmmm OptRegion_FixedAtoms {...}` if it hits the empty-$act_atom crash the
# earlier attempt hit.
! QM/XTB B97-3c ddCOSMO(Water) NumFreq TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{61 64 120 121 122 124 125 126 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136}
END
Charge_total 0
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job.xyz
